2 types of **saṁyoga** (**exam with example**) #\[\[**pāḷi** exam\]\]

**ekapada**saṁyoga: when the succeeding conjunct is in the same word - such as in **etth**a

such saṁyoga is pronounced short

**padantara- / nānāpada-**saṁyoga: when the succeeding conjunct is in the other term - such as in c**e tv**aṁ (maṁ ce tvaṁ nikhaṇaṁ vane)

such vowel is pronounced long

**note**:

when can short e and o be found in pāḷi?

when vaggantas or y / r / l / v are succeeding, the vowel is long - such as bhās**ey**ya (controversial)

in kaccāyana if a conjunct succeeds, the e / o are short

